==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege.als
    rationale: Clearing F_LeastPrivilege removes the constraint that a Success outcome must come from an allowed (role, kind) cell; the injection forces Alloy to construct exactly such a counterexample (a successful op whose caller's role is not in the permission matrix for the requested endpoint).
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_015_OnlyStaffDecide
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_OnlyStaffDecide: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditCompleteness lifts the rule that every application has its 'submitted' event (and the matching decision events). The injection forces an application with no SubmittedEv recorded, exactly the bug the assertion guards against.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_016_AuditTrail
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditTrail: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries removes the at-most-one-per-(app,type) rule on audit events. The injection forces two distinct ApplicationEvent rows for the same application and event type — the canonical 'someone overwrote/appended a duplicate audit row' bug.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OnePendingPerCustomer  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OnePendingPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Clearing F_OnePendingPerCustomer drops the partial-unique-index protection of FR-005. The injection forces two distinct Pending Review applications owned by the same customer, which is exactly the state FR-005 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer
      - FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedAccess  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedAccess.als
    rationale: Clearing F_OwnershipBasedAccess removes the rule that a customer's successful detail-read proves ownership. The injection forces a customer to receive a Success on GET /applications/{ref} for an application owned by a different customer — the cross-tenant leak FR-013/SC-004 forbid.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_013_CustomerSeesOnlyOwn
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_CustomerSeesOnlyOwn: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_StaffDecide  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_StaffDecide.als
    rationale: Clearing F_StaffDecide drops the role-of-decider invariant. The injection writes a Decision whose decider has the customer role, the exact privilege-escalation bug FR-015/SC-004 forbid.
    expected to FAIL: FR_015_OnlyStaffDecide
      - FR_015_OnlyStaffDecide: FAIL (expected)

